<title>UK: TENNIS-RAIN INTERRUPTS WIMBLEDON AGAIN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-RAIN INTERRUPTS WIMBLEDON AGAIN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Play at the Wimbledon tennis championships was interrupted by rain again on Tuesday.</p>
<p>As singles players battled for quarter-final places, there was a brief 10-minute stoppage around lunchtime.</p>
<p>Heavier rain in mid-afternoon again drove players from the courts and prospects looked more uncertain as the covers stayed firmly up.</p>
<p>Nearly three days were lost to the weather last week and the forecast remains unsettled.</p>
</text>
